    pr_ref:  # 2718
    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16 (round 9).**\n\n**Symptom.** On hypergumbo's self-analysis, the per-language file count disagrees between two layers of the same analysis:\n\n| Layer | bash file count | Source |\n|---|---:|---|\n| `profile.languages.bash.files` | 10 | `profile.py:_detect_languages` — extension scan with `DEFAULT_EXCLUDES` |\n| `analysis_runs[bash-v1].files_analyzed` | 41 | `bash-v1` analyzer pass |\n| `wc -l` ground truth (extensions, ALL dirs) | 40 | shell |\n| `wc -l` ground truth (extensions, with DEFAULT_EXCLUDES) | 10 | shell |\n\nThe two layers disagree by **4×** on what counts as a \"bash file\" in the same analysis run.\n\n**Root cause.** `profile.languages` applies `DEFAULT_EXCLUDES` (which excludes `.agent`, `.pytest_cache`, `.tox`, etc.) when enumerating files. The bash analyzer pass enumerates files through a different code path that does NOT apply the same exclude list — so it ends up analyzing `.sh` files inside `.agent/hooks/`, `.pytest_cache/`, etc.\n\nConcretely:\n- `find . \\( -path './.venv' -o -path '*/node_modules' -o -path './.git' -o -path './.agent' -o -path './.pytest_cache' \\) -prune -o -type f -name '*.sh' -print | wc -l` → 10 (matches profile)\n- `find . \\( -path './.venv' -o -path '*/node_modules' -o -path './.git' \\) -prune -o -type f -name '*.sh' -print | wc -l` → 40 (matches analyzer ±1 for shebang detection)\n\n**Invariant statement.** Within a single analysis run, every layer that counts or enumerates files for a given language must apply the same exclude policy. `profile.languages[L].files` and the count of files analyzed by the language-L analyzer pass must agree (modulo files the analyzer rejected for parse errors, which should be reported in `limits.failed_files`).\n\n**Severity.** Medium. This is observable on every multi-package repo with `.agent` or similar tooling directories. Consequences:\n- Agent consumer reads `profile.languages.bash.files = 10`, infers \"10 shell scripts in this repo\"\n- Same consumer reads `bash-v1.files_analyzed = 41` and gets a different number\n- Downstream tools that ratio language coverage (e.g., \"what fraction of files were analyzed?\") get nonsensical results\n- Edge counts / dead-code estimates that depend on the file count will be skewed\n\nLikely generalizes beyond bash: any language analyzer that does its own file enumeration risks this inconsistency. Verification needed for other languages.\n\n**Fix proposal — two viable approaches.**\n\n1. **Centralize file enumeration through `discovery.find_files()`** so every analyzer pass and the profile share the same exclude policy. This is the canonical fix.\n\n2. **Pass the file-list from profile to analyzers** so analyzers operate on the same set the profile already enumerated. Simpler but couples the two systems.\n\nRecommended: (1) — fixes at the source, prevents future regressions in new analyzers.\n\n**Test gap.** Property test: for each language L with a hypergumbo analyzer, assert `profile.languages[L].files >= len([r for r in analysis_runs if r.pass == f\"{L}-v1\"][0].files_analyzed)` (analyzer should never see MORE files than the profile reports) — and the reverse direction when no parse errors occurred.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/profile.py:737-768` (`_detect_languages`)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/discovery.py:393-460` (`DEFAULT_EXCLUDES`)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/bash.py` (bash analyzer — needs verification of its file-enum path)\n- `INV-tosum-...` (filed round 8 — `bash`/`shell` profile key duplication, sibling profile bug)\n- `INV-piroh-...` (filed round 5 — schema validation; related profile-output integrity)\n- `WI-soraj-...` (filed round 8 — `total_files` ambiguity; sibling \"what counts as a file?\" issue)"  # 2718
    fields:  # 2718
      statement: "Within a single analysis run, every layer that counts or enumerates files for a given language must apply the same exclude policy. profile.languages[L].files and the count of files analyzed by the language-L analyzer pass must agree (modulo files the analyzer rejected for parse errors, which should be reported in limits.failed_files)."  # 2718
      root_cause: "profile.languages applies DEFAULT_EXCLUDES (which excludes .agent, .pytest_cache, etc.) via discovery.find_files when enumerating files. The bash analyzer pass enumerates files through a different code path that does NOT apply the same exclude list, so it ends up analyzing .sh files inside .agent/hooks/, .pytest_cache/, etc. Likely generalizes beyond bash to any analyzer that does its own file enumeration."  # 2718
